        "body": "**omicverse 2.4.0** — https://pypi.org/project/omicverse/2.4.0/  ·  `pip install -U omicverse`\n\n42 commits since 2.3.2 — a multithreaded C++ backend becomes the default, plus new single-cell, spatial, bulk and imaging features and a round of performance work.\n\n### Multithreaded C++ backend (`backend='cpp'`, default)\n- **`backend=` / `ov.settings.backend`** on `qc`, `normalize_total`, `highly_variable_genes`, `preprocess`, `scale`, `pca`, `neighbors`, `umap`, `leiden`, `cosg`, `find_markers`, powered by [anndataoom-fast](https://pypi.org/project/anndataoom-fast/); `backend='python'` keeps the previous code; results independent of the thread count (#1022)\n- In memory and out of core: SEA-AD MTG (1.38M cells, 32 threads) standard workflow in 1.5 min with 13 GB peak memory\n- **Leiden** — brisc-style C++ Leiden by default under `cpp` (`flavor='leidenalg_exact'` for an exact leidenalg port); resolution lists in every mode (#1022, #1027)\n- **UMAP** — deterministic multithreaded layout; new `ov.pp.localmap` / `ov.pp.pacmap`\n- `find_markers(method='cosg')` streams from disk for AnnDataOOM (142 s / 105 GB → 2.1 s / 2.1 GB)\n\n### GPU mode\n- Works with rapids-singlecell 0.11–0.18; `neighbors(method=...)` no longer passed as the kNN algorithm (#1028)\n\n### Performance\n- pseudobulk up to 8.6x (#1026); AUCell 2.4x (#1025); `co_occurrence` memory 622 MB → 3.4 MB (#1024); scTenifoldKnk 24% (#1023)\n\n### Features\n- Single-cell: CellChat in PyTorch (`run_cellchat`); unified `run_ccc` (7 methods); dynamo perturbation backend; Scissor\n- Spatial: pluggable segmentation backends + seam-free tiling (#1001); `match_cells` / `register_images` (#999); marker-panel annotation (#1004)\n- Bulk & other: spike-in quantitative ChIP (#1021); `multisite_harmonize` (#1003); tumour/normal SNP-panel QC (#1020); pharmacophore-constrained docking (#1018); `fit_choice_model` (#1006); electrophysiology QC/ERP (#1002); radial cell annotation tree (#1019); ambient `method='envelope'` (#996)\n- pyedger from PyPI instead of a vendored copy (#986)\n\n### Fixes\n- ARPACK int32 overflow in UMAP spectral init at ~1.66M–2M cells (#990); TMM before voom in limma paths (#995); PCA no longer fits twice\n\nFull notes: https://github.com/omicverse/omicverse-tutorials/blob/main/docs/Release_notes.md\n",
